{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/429679-puella-magi-madoka-magica-a-must-watch-anime-inspiration-on-harrowings","id":429679,"title":"Puella Magi Madoka Magica: A MUST watch Anime Inspiration on Harrowings.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-05T20:17:03-08:00","id":429679,"title":"Puella Magi Madoka Magica: A MUST watch Anime Inspiration on Harrowings.","content":"Not for nothing is this Artistically Sublime, Epically Tragic and Deliciously Gothic smash-hit 2011 Anime Series called &quot;Card Captor Sakura in The World Of Darkness&quot;<br /> And it is a *must* watch for anyone seeking inspiration on how to create internalized, personal symbolic psychological Hells.<br /> <br /> I'll give an abridged version on the Tragedy of Miki Sayaka and another Fallen Hero to give you a rough idea of what you are in for<br /> But you are doing yourself a disservice NOT watching this *Masterpiece* (there is no other word for this work of art),<br /> Set aside 6 hours over a weekend and watch it NOW, and your Wraith (and indeed, World of Darkness) games will be richer for it.<br /> <br /> SPOILER ALERT<br /> <br /> Miki Sayaka was an adolescent duped into becoming a &quot;Puella Magi&quot; by a Catlike Genie-Creature called Kyubey,<br /> Who promised that byswearing to fight the Witches of the World to her dying days, any wish, no matter how impossible, can be fulfilled.<br /> The wish in question, is to heal the irreperably crippled hand of her Musical Prodigy crush Kyosuke, whose hand cannot even feel, much less play, his beloved violin<br /> All she has to do is to seperate her soul from her body, and condense it into a &quot;Soul Gem&quot;<br /> <br /> There is of course, no such thing as a free lunch.<br /> <br /> You see, withdrawing *so* much hope from the Universe to create a miracle of such magnitude does NOT sit well with the Kharmic Laws of the Universe, and<br /> Kharma demands payment WITH interest by turning the Soul Gem into a LITERAL depository of Despair (or Angst if you will for Wraith Players); each and EVERY Time the Puella Magi uses magic (ie, performs Miracles by withdrawing Hope from the Universe), she gets an equal deposit of Despair.<br /> <br /> Unless she periodically-deposits the LITERAL Dark Despair/Angst of her Soul into the &quot;Grief Seeds&quot; of the Witches she slays, her OWN soul will literally shatter with despair and hatch into a Witch<br /> <br /> As a Witch is a monster LITERALLY made of unfulfilled promises and broken dreams, her personal realm where she reigns supreme (appropriately called<br /> a &quot;Maze&quot; or &quot;Labyrinth&quot; if you will) is a twisted mockery of all the promises that which she was duped into selling her immortal soul for.<br /> <br /> Subject A: Miki Sayaka from above. Her timidness in voicing her love to the musical prodigy whom she gave everything to save, only to have him taken away<br /> distorted her soul into a gargantuan steampunk mermaid made of distorted bronze musical instruments (symbolically alluding to Hans Christian Anderson's &quot;Little Mermaid&quot;, another tale of futile sacrifice and one-sided love). Her Laybrinth, appropriately is populated by an omnipresent String Orchestra of faceless shadowy musicians, and written in runes floating from their Mourful Melodies are the cries of &quot;Look At Me! Why Don't You Notice Me?&quot;<br /> <br /> A master of a labyrinth literally made of unresolved issues, omnipotent yet trapped and damned.<br /> <br /> Subject B: Nagisa Momoe, a mere eight year old girl at the time of her transformation, was duped into wishing for a mere serving favorite snack, the cheesecake, over saving her terminally ill mother's life. Upon her damnation, her gluttony is made manifest as it distorts her into a bloated fanged catterpillar, ever munching ever eating within the hospital made of biscuits and cakes that is her prison. Her minions, abstract hybrids of doctors and medical instruments shaped in the style of Edvard Munch artwork, constantly taunt her for the greed that robbed her mother of salvation. Only through constantly gorging on snacks (and people) can she fill the void left by her loss. <br /> And as a final knife-twist, though she can create any snack at will, she is condemned to never dine or create the cheesecake, the *trifle* for which she sold her mother's life for.<br /> <br /> PHEW! That's a mouthful of an introduction for those unfamiliar with this Masterpiece (and Anime In General)<br /> <br /> But do yourself a favor and watch this series: Your Harrowings will be richer (and all the more frightening) for it all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The EXTENSIVE &quot;Madoka&quot; Fan Network (and of course, official websites) has an even more exhaustive database of backgrounds for the tragedy of all<br /> the Witches in the franchise; All The More Inspiration for you, Esteemed Fellow Storytellers.<br /> <br /> Now, Let The Harrowing Begin! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 03-10-2015, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T16:48:46-07:00","id":434854,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't this be more towards Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T17:52:47-07:00","id":434948,"title":"","content":"I fear Mage is the only one of the &quot;Big Three&quot; (or Big Five, if you count Wraith and Changeling) I have absolutely no familiarity with. (Sorry)<br /> <br /> I thought Madoka would be an appropriate source Material, as the &quot;Symbolic Personal Hell&quot; (Labyrinth) of the Witches In Question, created from the *literal* Despair/Angst and Broken-Hopes-And-Dreams of said fallen-heroes, is eerily similar to what happens when a Shadow induces Catharsis and drags it's Psyche down into their personal inner Hell. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T18:18:44-07:00","id":434968,"title":"","content":"I know little of Wraith, but that does seem an excellent connection to draw to Madoka. ^_^<br /> <br /> Likewise, I don't know as much about Mage, but I can certainly see it offering some inspiration there, as well. Really, it's impressive how rich it is in only 12 episodes. I think what lines it brings to mind could say some things about the gameline lenses one tends to use. For instance, I'm acquainted with Changeling: The Lost, and have the easiest time drawing parallels between someone becoming a Magical Girl through forging a Contract and ultimately becoming a Witch, and a mortal forging the contracts that will make of it a Changeling and then following the depressing path outlined in Equinox Road to become one of the Gentry. I'd agree the Wraith connection as you've described it is certainly more direct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}